From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 07:56:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] R74 report: the q6_K width cliffs are REFUTED at the served
 width, with the mechanism named

Timed decider, 1536 EXECUTED counterbalanced round-cells over 5 shapes, 8 widths, 4 arms. No new cell meets the pre-registered bar, so no default moves and no route cell changes. At n=5 every arm loses on the lm_head shape and the one positive cell is +2.0%, below the 3% bar - which step 0 predicted: the n=5 step has no static signature at all. At n=6 both reshapes win on two shapes and lose on the others, and NUM_ROWS carries no shape term, so the cell cannot be expressed. The CHECK-R71 'try ROWS_FROM=8 first' hypothesis is answered and inverted: rows 1 removes only part of the MMVQ n=5 cliff and destroys the shipped n=7,8 win, so the static 4-row shape is the CAUSE of that win. Adds the two registry rows and the gate receipts.

Origin: lane-258 / R74 brief steps 2-5
Measured-effect: none served (nothing ships a default); decider 1536 round-cells, gates 261 targeted + 1004 MUL_MAT_ID cases EXECUTED
Lane: lane-258
Cherry-picked-from: e853d55422b46619a9cffd0a17091cf6d1e9a869
---
 docs/OPTIONS-REGISTRY.md | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

